From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:40:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: apple,pmgr-pwrstate: add
 apple,sleep-driver-owned

After a firmware-driven suspend the power controller puts each domain
back where genpd's books have it. Some domains need their driver's order
on the way back instead: the GPU's needs its target, then its bridge,
and only then automatic power management. Let the tree mark such a
domain, so that the power controller leaves it to its driver after a
wake.

Signed-off-by: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>

(cherry picked from commit ab67f7e75c6b922918dc42ccfed2eaef10eb8816)

[deep-sleep-2: our consumer-switched rule (requires apple,firmware-owned) kept instead of Aurora's forbidden-property list; apple,sleep-driver-owned property added]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5

(cherry picked from commit 9e84249fd673dc50a5beff0cf9f4629f809f01df)
(cherry picked from commit 984f7f9795aefb6694c60b4dc64eec7f6f68d3d6)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-pwrstate.yaml     | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-pwrstate.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-pwrstate.yaml
index d9cf0b9129..20a0c28f81 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-pwrstate.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-pwrstate.yaml
@@ -122,6 +122,13 @@ properties:
       system sleep. Runtime power management is unaffected.
     type: boolean
 
+  apple,sleep-driver-owned:
+    description:
+      The driver behind this domain lowers it before a system sleep and brings
+      it back afterwards, in an order its hardware needs. The power controller
+      leaves it alone after a wake.
+    type: boolean
+
   apple,firmware-owned:
     description:
       The boot loader hands over active hardware whose power domain remains
